			},
			"date": "2025-07-14T17:13:16.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> lightning abstracts away a bunch of complexity in how it dynamically reassigns pins depending on the task, but in general as a user i can plug it in and it works, whereas USB-C attempts to do so much more than lightning ever did, and as a result as a user I need to be aware of the power and data throughput capabilities of the two devices as well as the cable itself</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
